Z||000000||87GTJohn||05-27-2000||02:28 PM||||Bought a 88 GT Auto about two weeks ago, someone had placed black tape over the "service engine" light.  Removed tape and guess what? Code 32 and 44.  Check EGR valve (works) trace vacuum lines (burnt through). One down, one to go, Check OS (appears good), check more vacuum lines, one the connects into upper plenum (burnt through).  Trip to store, rubber vacuum line .25 a foot, buy 10 feet (never know).  Cut out old burnt parts and splice with rubber line.  Run engine, no codes, cool.  I think I got off cheap, total cost to fix about .25 cents.  Gotta love my fiero's (87GT, 88GT).<BR>John     ||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||05-27-2000||02:46 PM||||good work but if i was you i would change ot all liines with rubber, i did this and now i don't have to worry if a plastic line is torn.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||05-27-2000||04:42 PM||||The tape trick is so pathetic.... I had a car where the previous owner did the same thing. I was p*ssed!  Mostly at myself for not noticing...||||reg||1
Z||000003||TalShino||05-28-2000||12:51 AM||||I know this is differant story, but I thought about warning lights... and I thought of something, a warning light I hate seeing, that check speedo light.. you know the blinking blue lights in ya rearview.. hehe.. dont ya'll hate em?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>55 in a 45.. no ticket! Thank God!||||reg||1
